{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And he took curd and milk, etc.</b> This teaches that he fed them meat and milk. And when the Holy One, blessed be He, wished to give the Torah to Israel, the angels said: ״תנה הודך על השמים״. He said to them: It is written in the Torah, ״לא תבשל גדי בחלב אמו״ — and you, when you came down below, ate meat and milk, as it is said: ״ויקח חמאה וחלב״. Immediately they gave praise to the Holy One, blessed be He. And this is what is written in the chapter כי תשא: ״כי על פי הדברים האלה כרתי״ etc., and it is written just before it: ״לא תבשל גדי בחלב אמו״. And this midrash disagrees with another midrash: our father Abraham, peace be upon him, fulfilled even עירובי תבשילין — meaning mixed dishes, that he would not eat meat with milk, nor even meat and afterwards milk, but rather milk and afterwards meat, as it is written: ״ויקח חמאה וחלב״ and afterwards ״ואת בן הבקר אשר עשה״. And so Rashi also explained: one by one, that he prepared [them] and brought [them] before them." "<b>And the calf that he made.</b> Meaning: he prepared and arranged it — as in ״ויעש אלהים את הרקיע״, which Rashi explained in the sense of preparation." "<b>And they ate.</b> Meaning: they would burn up the food, from the language of ״והסנה איננו אוכל״ — it is not consumed, it is not burned."], :book :genesis, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:05:34.418459278Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}